# gaming — the "gaming edition in one image" pack (#25, PROPOSAL §14). Steam,
# Lutris, Heroic, the GameMode/MangoHud overlay stack, gamescope, and a
# Proton-GE build for titles upstream Proton can't run. Installed ONLINE on
# demand (official repos via pacman, AUR via paru) — nothing here is baked or
# stashed in the ISO (design pivot #42); only this name-list rides as TEXT.
#
# multilib is ALREADY enabled in the installed-target pacman.conf
# (overlay/airootfs/etc/pacman.conf ships a live [multilib] block), so the
# 32-bit members are declared DIRECTLY — there is deliberately NO multilib
# toggle (§14 audit fix a; validate.sh forbids one). pacman just resolves the
# lib32-* names against the already-enabled repo.
#
# post-add writes the sentinel-fenced game-mode toggle widget launch line into
# ~/.config/hypr/custom/execs.lua (via ii_lua_block_write, guarded behind the
# widget's presence so non-pack users never get a dead launcher); post-remove
# strips it. The widget QML itself is framework work (out of scope here).
#meta:type gaming
steam
lutris
heroic-games-launcher
gamemode
lib32-gamemode
mangohud
lib32-mangohud
gamescope
# Proton-GE — community Proton build (AUR; built at runtime via paru).
proton-ge-custom-bin
